From 4b339666411b3ae94791b01a0fdd33bd7233af34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lierfang Support Team <itsupport@lierfang.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:55:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ui/rdp: send audio from any audiodev to the RDP client

Tap the mixed output of the sound card's backend with
AUD_add_capture(), like the VNC audio extension, so "-audiodev none",
"pa", "spice"... all reach the RDP client. The new "audiodev=" option
picks the backend; without it the VM's only audiodev is used, and with
several a warning asks for the option. A sound card on "-audiodev rdp"
is still forwarded directly and is not captured.

audio.c gains audio_get_sole_audio_state() and audio_state_driver():
the list of audio states is private to it.

Signed-off-by: Lierfang Support Team <itsupport@lierfang.com>
